1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[English subtitles are available]

2
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:12,230
[Kakarayan created
everything in the world]

3
00:00:12,310 --> 00:00:18,780
[and loved everything that He has made.]

4
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:24,810
[As time went by,]

5
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:28,070
[year after year,]

6
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:32,470
[with Kakarayan's favor,]

7
00:00:32,549 --> 00:00:37,350
[humans started to think]

8
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:40,520
[that they were as great as Kakarayan.]

9
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:45,270
[One by one,
they slowly forgot who Kakarayan was.]

10
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:50,110
[Humans had stained the rivers,
polluted the oceans,]

11
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:55,120
[hurt the mountains,
and cut down the trees.]

12
00:00:55,210 --> 00:00:58,420
[Because of the humans,]

13
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,860
[the world was no longer as wonderful]

14
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:07,050
[as what Kakarayan had initially made.]

15
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:09,730
[Kakarayan became upset]

16
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:13,560
[due to human ego]

17
00:01:13,650 --> 00:01:21,520
[and His unconditional love for humanity.]

18
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:24,160
[So Kakarayan]

19
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:27,860
[told Himself a lie.]

20
00:01:27,950 --> 00:01:30,760
[In that lie,]

21
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:35,910
[there was a person
who became His messenger.]

22
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,590
[He would travel the world in His place]

23
00:01:38,729 --> 00:01:43,920
[to protect the world
that He created on His behalf.]

24
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:02,970
I really envy the Kawas.

25
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:05,040
You don't have to work.

26
00:02:09,130 --> 00:02:11,370
Who said I don't have to work?

27
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:13,880
I'm working right now.

28
00:02:13,970 --> 00:02:16,260
Yes, your job

29
00:02:16,350 --> 00:02:18,280
is to play kendama.

30
00:02:18,370 --> 00:02:19,340
And...

31
00:02:20,310 --> 00:02:21,980
to protect me?

32
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:24,050
Do you think my job

33
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:25,810
is only to protect you?

34
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:28,970
I have a bunch of work to do
as the messenger of Kakarayan.

35
00:02:30,030 --> 00:02:31,480
Like what?

36
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:33,420
I have to make sure

37
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:34,690
that everything shown
in the Reflection of Time

38
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:37,600
goes according to Kakarayan's plan.

39
00:02:37,730 --> 00:02:39,620
I also have to give all of you
blessings or calamities

40
00:02:39,710 --> 00:02:41,640
according to Kakarayan's will.

41
00:02:42,790 --> 00:02:44,990
Blessings or calamities?

42
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:48,860
I mean the rain.

43
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:53,130
I see.

44
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:56,560
I also have another very important job.

45
00:02:56,650 --> 00:02:58,280
Do you want to know what it is?

46
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:02,850
On behalf of Kakarayan,

47
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:05,980
I help name all the Kawas.

48
00:03:08,130 --> 00:03:10,330
You name them?

49
00:03:33,650 --> 00:03:35,150
Do you know who you are?

50
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:39,810
Then do you know why you're here

51
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:41,660
and what your name is?

52
00:03:48,430 --> 00:03:50,329
Your name is Falo, the goddess of flower.

53
00:03:50,410 --> 00:03:53,630
Falo.

54
00:03:53,710 --> 00:03:55,300
Yes, Falo.

55
00:03:57,190 --> 00:03:57,940
Falo.

56
00:03:59,430 --> 00:04:00,710
From now on,

57
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:03,170
you shall receive
the blessings of Kakarayan.

58
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:06,820
Your future duty

59
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:09,730
is to protect this path

60
00:04:10,210 --> 00:04:13,380
and bless everyone who walks on it.

61
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:33,310
Listen to me carefully.

62
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:35,600
Remember your name.

63
00:04:36,390 --> 00:04:37,890
Most importantly,

64
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:40,570
follow the blessings of Kakarayan

65
00:04:41,450 --> 00:04:44,220
to become a Kawas that blesses the people.

66
00:05:03,010 --> 00:05:04,370
[Before we come up with a name,]

67
00:05:04,460 --> 00:05:06,970
we call them Papa' orip.

68
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:10,750
It's something
between a Kawas and a Kariah,

69
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:12,340
a form of consciousness.

70
00:05:12,430 --> 00:05:14,140
Kakarayan hasn't given His blessing yet,

71
00:05:14,270 --> 00:05:15,550
so they don't know

72
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:18,010
their purpose of coming into this world

73
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:20,210
until I give them names.

74
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:23,690
That's how they become Kawas
that bless the humans.

75
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:26,900
So the names of all the Kawas in the world

76
00:05:26,990 --> 00:05:28,840
were given by you?

77
00:05:29,060 --> 00:05:29,810
Yes.

78
00:05:33,110 --> 00:05:35,700
What will happen

79
00:05:35,790 --> 00:05:36,800
if you don't give them a name?

80
00:05:38,030 --> 00:05:40,010
Then their future will be uncertain

81
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:42,210
and become variables of the world.

82
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:44,240
They may be good.

83
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:46,790
But they could also be bad.

84
00:05:48,990 --> 00:05:50,570
What do you mean

85
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:55,020
by a bad Papa 'orip?

86
00:05:58,540 --> 00:05:59,770
[Breaking news.]

87
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:01,040
[At Minshin Road, Taipei...]

88
00:06:01,130 --> 00:06:02,890
Pu is ridiculous.

89
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:03,990
I told him to get a spot first,

90
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:05,530
but he's nowhere to be seen.

91
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:07,030
Is he a turtle or something?

92
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:09,580
[They fell unconscious on the ground.]

93
00:06:09,670 --> 00:06:10,810
Yi-han.

94
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:12,840
Look at the news.

95
00:06:12,970 --> 00:06:13,720
What?

96
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:15,650
[Like a domino effect,]

97
00:06:15,740 --> 00:06:17,240
[people are collapsing
after losing consciousness.]

98
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:18,160
[As this happened]

99
00:06:18,250 --> 00:06:20,270
[at a busy intersection,]

100
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:22,120
[the effects are spreading fast.]

101
00:06:22,210 --> 00:06:24,060
[The two pavements
on either side of the road]

102
00:06:23,750 --> 00:06:26,170
[Latest News,
Hundreds collapsed for no reason]

103
00:06:24,190 --> 00:06:25,290
[and the shops nearby...]

104
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:26,780
Didn't we just pass by

105
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,680
the area mentioned on the news?

106
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:29,820
[The police at the scene]

107
00:06:29,950 --> 00:06:31,620
[didn't detect any toxic reaction.]

108
00:06:31,710 --> 00:06:32,720
[Moreover, the area]

109
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:34,570
[is a commercial and residential area.]

110
00:06:34,659 --> 00:06:36,070
[Preliminary investigations
have eliminated]

111
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:38,620
[the possibility of a gas leak.]

112
00:06:45,390 --> 00:06:46,630
Tien-ti!

113
00:06:53,710 --> 00:06:57,450
♫ But I won't hold an umbrella ♫

114
00:06:57,580 --> 00:07:02,110
♫ So that I can feel your presence ♫

115
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:02,820
He's right there. Can't you see him?

116
00:07:02,910 --> 00:07:04,310
That kid suddenly ran out.

117
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:06,950
That's why I stopped, okay?

118
00:07:19,630 --> 00:07:20,240
Tell the EMT

119
00:07:20,330 --> 00:07:21,780
that we can't accept patients anymore.

120
00:07:21,870 --> 00:07:22,700
Okay?

121
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,020
Yes. Thank you.

122
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:28,200
Hold it tight.

123
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:35,860
Here.

124
00:07:37,180 --> 00:07:39,640
Ma'am.

125
00:07:39,730 --> 00:07:41,710
You can continue later.

126
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:45,360
Madam!

127
00:07:45,450 --> 00:07:46,510
We have four patients coming in.

128
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:47,870
They'll be here in five minutes.

129
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:49,630
They're all from Minshin Road.

130
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:50,730
All of them have trouble breathing

131
00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:52,400
and are unconscious.

132
00:07:52,490 --> 00:07:54,080
Our beds are already full.

133
00:07:54,159 --> 00:07:54,909
Forget about the ventilators,

134
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:55,920
we don't even have

135
00:07:56,010 --> 00:07:56,940
enough respirators.

136
00:07:57,020 --> 00:07:58,170
Can't they be sent to another hospital?

137
00:07:58,260 --> 00:08:00,100
All the other hospitals are full.

138
00:08:00,190 --> 00:08:00,980
It's okay. Listen here.

139
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,350
Go up to the ward and ask

140
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:03,930
if we can send them up. Go now!

141
00:08:04,020 --> 00:08:07,060
-Okay.
-Madam!

142
00:08:07,190 --> 00:08:09,120
We have two more patients
from Zhongzheng Hospital,

143
00:08:09,210 --> 00:08:10,220
an adult and a child.

144
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:11,980
Respiratory asthma
and blood oxygen level two.

145
00:08:12,070 --> 00:08:13,790
They are also
from the accident on Minshin Road.

146
00:08:13,870 --> 00:08:15,370
I just talked to the EMT about it.

147
00:08:16,030 --> 00:08:16,690
Hold on!

148
00:08:16,820 --> 00:08:17,790
Stop taking pictures!

149
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:19,070
Excuse me!

150
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:20,340
Excuse me!

151
00:08:20,430 --> 00:08:21,350
That way!

152
00:08:21,440 --> 00:08:22,720
-Move aside!
-Stop taking pictures!

153
00:10:03,740 --> 00:10:05,720
[Emergency]

154
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:06,510
This way.

155
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:08,050
This way.

156
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:09,850
Please make way!

157
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:12,450
Make way, reporters!

158
00:10:10,290 --> 00:10:16,230
[Episode 9, Between the World and You,
I Choose You]

159
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:13,510
Let us through!

160
00:10:13,590 --> 00:10:15,710
Please make way!

161
00:10:15,790 --> 00:10:17,470
You've reached the hospital.

162
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:51,040
Don't be so anxious, Wu Yi-han.

163
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:52,880
Calm down.

164
00:10:54,420 --> 00:10:56,050
Yes.

165
00:10:57,110 --> 00:10:58,250
Think about it.

166
00:10:58,380 --> 00:10:59,660
If we go to the restaurant

167
00:10:59,790 --> 00:11:01,730
from our office,

168
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:04,540
it's in the opposite direction
of the intersection.

169
00:11:07,270 --> 00:11:09,160
Something came up. Don't cry.

170
00:11:09,250 --> 00:11:11,280
All right, that's all for now. Bye.

171
00:11:11,410 --> 00:11:12,730
How did it go?

172
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:15,020
Did you find the woman who sang the song?

173
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:16,200
No.

174
00:11:16,290 --> 00:11:18,490
She was already gone
when I went back there.

175
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:23,110
I just remembered something.

176
00:11:23,460 --> 00:11:25,180
That singer

177
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:27,770
and the little boy I saw

178
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:30,460
when we were riding the bike

179
00:11:30,590 --> 00:11:32,090
must be the thing you and Grandma
told me about.

180
00:11:32,170 --> 00:11:34,640
They're neither Kawas nor Kariah.

181
00:11:34,730 --> 00:11:36,050
-They must be Papa' orip.
-Papa' orip.

182
00:11:36,130 --> 00:11:36,970
Yes.

183
00:11:37,060 --> 00:11:37,890
I know those two

184
00:11:37,980 --> 00:11:39,740
look completely different.

185
00:11:39,830 --> 00:11:44,190
But from the way they looked at me,

186
00:11:44,270 --> 00:11:46,120
I'm very sure they're the same person.

187
00:11:49,420 --> 00:11:51,580
I just saw the news.

188
00:11:51,710 --> 00:11:53,820
It's not just the intersection.

189
00:11:53,950 --> 00:11:56,510
A lot of people nearby also fainted.

190
00:11:56,590 --> 00:11:58,970
The hospitals are packed.

191
00:11:59,060 --> 00:12:00,820
Pu is in one of them too.

192
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:05,090
Then...

193
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:06,490
is he...

194
00:12:13,270 --> 00:12:14,330
It's okay.

195
00:12:15,950 --> 00:12:17,620
The most important thing right now

196
00:12:17,710 --> 00:12:20,040
is you've regained all of your powers.

197
00:12:20,180 --> 00:12:21,760
If all these mishaps happened

198
00:12:21,850 --> 00:12:24,530
because of that Papa' orip,

199
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:27,080
does that mean

200
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:29,150
you can save them?

201
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:30,340
You can cure Pu.

202
00:12:30,430 --> 00:12:32,540
You can also save everyone
who has been hurt.

203
00:12:32,630 --> 00:12:33,380
Am I right?

204
00:12:37,470 --> 00:12:39,490
Who are you to save him?

205
00:12:39,580 --> 00:12:40,770
Are you saving him as a friend

206
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:42,310
or as the messenger of Kakarayan?

207
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:44,600
Or do you already

208
00:12:44,730 --> 00:12:47,190
think of yourself as Kakarayan?

209
00:12:58,020 --> 00:13:03,250
If you can hear me,

210
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:08,620
if you're still willing
to bless this world,

211
00:13:08,750 --> 00:13:13,940
if you haven't given up on them,

212
00:13:14,030 --> 00:13:19,130
if you haven't given up on us...

213
00:13:46,020 --> 00:13:51,170
[If You haven't given up on us...]

214
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:55,920
[You said you saw the doomsday again?]

215
00:13:58,340 --> 00:14:00,100
When I tried to save Pu,

216
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:02,740
Kakarayan showed me

217
00:14:02,820 --> 00:14:04,540
the Reflection of Time
of the doomsday again.

218
00:15:02,750 --> 00:15:03,720
Hello.

219
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,820
Look at them.

220
00:15:08,910 --> 00:15:11,370
Don't they look happy?

221
00:15:11,510 --> 00:15:13,710
Do you want to be happy like them?

222
00:15:13,790 --> 00:15:16,570
Go on, go get it.

223
00:15:16,650 --> 00:15:18,370
If you want to be happy, go get it.

224
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:20,970
Get it from them.

225
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:23,430
That's how people of this world

226
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:24,930
do it anyway.

227
00:15:35,130 --> 00:15:36,540
No-no, what's wrong?

228
00:15:36,630 --> 00:15:40,540
No-no.

229
00:15:40,630 --> 00:15:41,950
Wake up, No-no.

230
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:42,880
No-no.

231
00:15:43,010 --> 00:15:44,810
Wait here. I'll get the teacher.

232
00:15:44,940 --> 00:15:46,400
No-no.

233
00:15:59,990 --> 00:16:01,310
I've talked

234
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:02,720
to Pu's family.

235
00:16:02,810 --> 00:16:04,740
He's currently unconscious.

236
00:16:06,640 --> 00:16:08,700
But here is the good news.

237
00:16:08,790 --> 00:16:10,510
It's not life-threatening for now.

238
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:12,880
At this critical time,

239
00:16:12,970 --> 00:16:14,030
I hope every one of you

240
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,440
will take care of yourself.

241
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:17,940
I don't want anymore accidents.

242
00:16:20,450 --> 00:16:21,950
It's all my fault.

243
00:16:23,310 --> 00:16:26,170
If I hadn't asked Pu to get in line,

244
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:28,190
he wouldn't be in the hospital right now.

245
00:16:29,690 --> 00:16:31,190
I'm sorry.

246
00:16:32,150 --> 00:16:35,500
Yi-han, don't think too much.

247
00:16:35,590 --> 00:16:36,950
It's going to be okay.

248
00:16:40,870 --> 00:16:43,110
Although he's still unconscious,

249
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:45,350
let's keep our spirits up

250
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:47,200
and do our job properly.

251
00:16:47,290 --> 00:16:48,790
Let's cheer for him.

252
00:16:49,450 --> 00:16:50,410
Can you do that?

253
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:07,000
What does saving Pu

254
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:09,250
have anything to do

255
00:17:09,329 --> 00:17:10,700
with the Reflection of Time that you saw?

256
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:14,349
Haven't you seen
what doomsday looked like?

257
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:15,270
Then why?

258
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:17,079
Because compared to saving them,

259
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,400
I'd rather want to protect

260
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:20,990
the Reflection of Time.

261
00:17:24,599 --> 00:17:26,579
Because the Reflection of Time that I saw

262
00:17:28,079 --> 00:17:30,500
is different from the one

263
00:17:30,580 --> 00:17:32,040
[of the doomsday from before.]

264
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:58,080
[In that empty doomsday,]

265
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:01,870
[I saw you.]

266
00:18:02,830 --> 00:18:04,290
[You saw me]

267
00:18:04,420 --> 00:18:07,230
in the Reflection of Time of the doomsday?

268
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:10,090
I don't understand.

269
00:18:12,120 --> 00:18:13,530
According to the original
Reflection of Time

270
00:18:13,610 --> 00:18:15,240
that you saw,

271
00:18:15,330 --> 00:18:17,180
I should've passed away

272
00:18:17,270 --> 00:18:19,470
on the day of the last rainfall

273
00:18:19,550 --> 00:18:20,920
due to an accident

274
00:18:21,010 --> 00:18:23,600
at that intersection, right?

275
00:18:23,730 --> 00:18:26,240
Then why did you...

276
00:18:30,690 --> 00:18:32,930
Did we change the Reflection of Time?

277
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:34,870
Have we really changed the future?

278
00:18:36,050 --> 00:18:38,560
If the future can really be changed,

279
00:18:39,270 --> 00:18:41,290
then we have a chance.

280
00:18:41,380 --> 00:18:43,010
As long as we find a way,

281
00:18:43,140 --> 00:18:44,850
maybe we can even change

282
00:18:44,990 --> 00:18:46,310
this Reflection of Time of the doomsday.

283
00:18:46,440 --> 00:18:48,500
No, I can't.

284
00:18:48,590 --> 00:18:49,520
Why not?

285
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:51,100
I've told you many times.

286
00:18:51,190 --> 00:18:52,600
The end of the world

287
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:54,880
is caused by you humans.

288
00:18:54,970 --> 00:18:57,440
Kakarayan only took back His blessings.

289
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:00,740
And I'm just His messenger.

290
00:19:00,820 --> 00:19:01,840
There's no way for me

291
00:19:01,920 --> 00:19:02,580
to change anything by myself.

292
00:19:02,670 --> 00:19:04,340
But if we don't try...

293
00:19:04,480 --> 00:19:06,980
-I...
-The reason you're still here

294
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:10,020
is because I made a wish to Kakarayan.

295
00:19:10,150 --> 00:19:13,360
He answered it and gave me His blessing.

296
00:19:13,450 --> 00:19:15,780
He reinstated me as the messenger.

297
00:19:29,950 --> 00:19:33,250
If you can hear my voice,

298
00:19:35,540 --> 00:19:36,680
please let me see her

299
00:19:37,740 --> 00:19:41,300
as soon as I open my eyes.

300
00:19:57,320 --> 00:19:59,300
Kakarayan never changed His plan

301
00:19:59,430 --> 00:20:01,190
for anyone.

302
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:03,480
But this time, He granted my wish.

303
00:20:03,570 --> 00:20:04,230
I really can't

304
00:20:04,310 --> 00:20:06,470
be greedy like you humans

305
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:08,450
and ask more from Him.

306
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:10,120
What if He changes His mind?

307
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:11,310
What should I do

308
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:12,760
if He retracts my wish?

309
00:20:12,850 --> 00:20:13,730
But...

310
00:20:13,820 --> 00:20:15,400
Don't you get it?

311
00:20:15,490 --> 00:20:16,330
I don't care

312
00:20:16,410 --> 00:20:18,090
what will happen to the world.

313
00:20:19,450 --> 00:20:21,210
Because between the world and you,

314
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:24,640
I choose you.

315
00:20:53,240 --> 00:20:55,220
Will I be cured

316
00:20:55,920 --> 00:20:58,080
after the surgery tomorrow?

317
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:02,920
Or is this surgery

318
00:21:03,010 --> 00:21:04,900
not going to change anything?

319
00:21:06,480 --> 00:21:09,040
Is it just to buy me time?

320
00:21:11,590 --> 00:21:13,170
I thought

321
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:16,430
that if this trip went well,

322
00:21:16,510 --> 00:21:19,950
I could go further away next time.

323
00:21:21,620 --> 00:21:23,110
And after next time,

324
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:26,850
I could go further and further away.

325
00:21:30,590 --> 00:21:32,930
But I never thought

326
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:36,840
that I could even mess up

327
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:39,790
a simple three-day trip.

328
00:21:42,740 --> 00:21:46,610
Sung-en, don't think like that.

329
00:21:48,590 --> 00:21:52,770
I'm sure you'll recover soon.

330
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:58,180
Then you'll be able to go

331
00:21:59,410 --> 00:22:01,220
wherever you want.

332
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:05,220
Mom.

333
00:22:07,020 --> 00:22:08,610
What should I do?

334
00:22:11,160 --> 00:22:12,130
I thought

335
00:22:12,260 --> 00:22:15,870
I was prepared for this.

336
00:22:17,540 --> 00:22:21,980
But when I heard
that I have another surgery to do,

337
00:22:24,010 --> 00:22:25,860
I'm still scared.

338
00:22:28,060 --> 00:22:30,210
I really can't accept it.

339
00:22:32,540 --> 00:22:34,260
Why me?

340
00:22:36,940 --> 00:22:38,260
Why?

341
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:40,820
Why is God doing this to me?

342
00:22:43,100 --> 00:22:45,920
There's still so much I want to do.

343
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:54,230
If possible, I really wish...

344
00:22:54,890 --> 00:22:56,130
I wish

345
00:22:56,210 --> 00:22:58,770
someone could switch their lives

346
00:22:59,910 --> 00:23:01,540
or their bodies with me.

347
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:05,760
I really can't bear

348
00:23:05,850 --> 00:23:08,840
to lie down here like this anymore.

349
00:24:00,500 --> 00:24:01,820
Carry me, Dad.

350
00:24:04,190 --> 00:24:06,040
Be careful, my dear.

351
00:24:06,170 --> 00:24:07,230
Come on.

352
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:08,990
Le-le, come here.

353
00:24:09,120 --> 00:24:10,260
Be careful.

354
00:24:10,350 --> 00:24:11,670
Dad, I'm slipping.

355
00:24:11,760 --> 00:24:13,390
Okay. Be careful.

356
00:24:14,310 --> 00:24:17,220
Be careful.

357
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:21,310
Honey, can you help her?

358
00:24:22,450 --> 00:24:22,720
Okay.

359
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:24,920
Hold her.

360
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:27,160
-Here, I'll record it for you.
-Is it fun?

361
00:24:27,250 --> 00:24:28,480
-Okay, look at Mom.
-Okay, look over here.

362
00:24:28,570 --> 00:24:29,050
Look at Mom.

363
00:24:29,140 --> 00:24:30,810
[Go get it.]

364
00:24:30,900 --> 00:24:33,140
[If you want to be happy, go get it.]

365
00:25:21,800 --> 00:25:26,340
[Is it contagious?
There are many questions]

366
00:25:32,100 --> 00:25:34,120
['Orad. Where are you?]

367
00:25:34,390 --> 00:25:35,180
[I'm here.]

368
00:26:02,550 --> 00:26:04,840
Although 'Orad made his choice

369
00:26:05,760 --> 00:26:07,390
to let you remain here,

370
00:26:07,780 --> 00:26:09,100
that doesn't mean

371
00:26:10,200 --> 00:26:12,230
I'm on the same page as him.

372
00:26:22,570 --> 00:26:24,850
So are you here to take me away

373
00:26:26,350 --> 00:26:28,990
to rectify anything that's divergent
from Kakarayan's plan?

374
00:26:30,220 --> 00:26:31,980
Why does it seem like

375
00:26:33,080 --> 00:26:35,630
you're no longer afraid or hesitant?

376
00:26:38,800 --> 00:26:40,300
Because I just asked 'Orad

377
00:26:41,130 --> 00:26:43,110
to take me to see you.

378
00:26:46,940 --> 00:26:48,000
You wanted to see me?

379
00:26:50,110 --> 00:26:51,340
Your job

380
00:26:52,220 --> 00:26:53,370
is to correct

381
00:26:53,450 --> 00:26:56,090
anything that differs
from Kakarayan's plan, isn't it?

382
00:26:57,770 --> 00:26:59,260
So you should know

383
00:27:00,270 --> 00:27:02,120
how I can meet Kakarayan, right?

384
00:27:04,190 --> 00:27:06,080
You want to meet Kakarayan?

385
00:27:06,170 --> 00:27:07,180
Why?

386
00:27:10,520 --> 00:27:12,590
'Orad has made his choice.

387
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:13,740
For my sake,

388
00:27:14,130 --> 00:27:16,460
he chose not to change the future he saw.

389
00:27:17,700 --> 00:27:20,160
But I also have a choice
that I want to make.

390
00:27:23,020 --> 00:27:24,820
Take me to Kakarayan.

391
00:27:25,660 --> 00:27:27,020
I want to ask Him

392
00:27:27,680 --> 00:27:28,960
to save Sung-en.

393
00:27:30,540 --> 00:27:32,350
I want to ask Him to stop

394
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:34,810
the Papa' orip that is harming humans.

395
00:27:35,560 --> 00:27:36,970
I want to ask Him

396
00:27:37,980 --> 00:27:41,680
to save the innocent people
who have fallen unconscious.

397
00:27:42,820 --> 00:27:44,930
I don't know if I should call you naive

398
00:27:45,060 --> 00:27:46,740
or greedy.

399
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:49,900
Do you really think
that by meeting Kakarayan,

400
00:27:49,990 --> 00:27:52,370
He will do what you ask?

401
00:27:55,140 --> 00:27:56,460
But how would I know

402
00:27:56,550 --> 00:27:57,730
if I don't try?

403
00:28:00,810 --> 00:28:03,010
It's okay if He doesn't agree.

404
00:28:03,450 --> 00:28:05,040
At least when I see Him,

405
00:28:05,740 --> 00:28:07,020
I can ask Him face-to-face

406
00:28:07,110 --> 00:28:08,250
about everything.

407
00:28:10,050 --> 00:28:11,510
What do you want to ask Him?

408
00:28:13,530 --> 00:28:16,040
I don't understand why He's such a loser.

409
00:28:17,750 --> 00:28:20,130
He was the one who arranged this.

410
00:28:20,220 --> 00:28:21,890
So why doesn't He do it Himself?

411
00:28:23,470 --> 00:28:26,470
He left a pile of dirty work
for 'Orad to clean up.

412
00:28:26,550 --> 00:28:28,530
And now, He's hiding.

413
00:28:30,030 --> 00:28:32,190
He's hiding so that no one can find Him.

414
00:28:34,300 --> 00:28:35,530
It doesn't make sense, does it?

415
00:28:35,620 --> 00:28:38,390
Isn't He the greatest God in the world?

416
00:28:38,480 --> 00:28:39,880
How can He be so irresponsible?

417
00:28:40,020 --> 00:28:41,380
He has no sense of duty.

418
00:28:45,910 --> 00:28:47,360
I'm laughing

419
00:28:47,940 --> 00:28:48,990
because I'd also like to know

420
00:28:49,480 --> 00:28:50,660
how He's going to answer

421
00:28:50,750 --> 00:28:51,900
those questions.

422
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:54,930
You want to meet Kakarayan so badly?

423
00:28:55,060 --> 00:28:57,350
Okay, I'll bring you to him.

424
00:28:59,200 --> 00:29:01,800
The door leads straight to Pinokayan.

425
00:29:02,630 --> 00:29:04,220
You want to meet Kakarayan

426
00:29:04,350 --> 00:29:06,110
to find out the truth.

427
00:29:08,220 --> 00:29:11,080
Go through the door and you'll meet Him.

428
00:29:17,590 --> 00:29:19,310
Once I go through this door,

429
00:29:20,320 --> 00:29:22,340
I'll be able to meet Kakarayan?

430
00:29:22,650 --> 00:29:23,310
Yes.

431
00:29:25,640 --> 00:29:29,600
You can then ask Him personally

432
00:29:30,040 --> 00:29:31,490
about what you wish to know.

433
00:30:20,510 --> 00:30:22,140
Don't go any further.

434
00:30:27,240 --> 00:30:28,380
This...

435
00:30:30,720 --> 00:30:33,310
It's where I went after the accident.

436
00:30:34,190 --> 00:30:35,340
Why am I...

437
00:30:36,440 --> 00:30:38,060
Why am I here again?

438
00:30:42,110 --> 00:30:43,260
[Don't be afraid.]

439
00:30:43,340 --> 00:30:45,100
[It's just a nightmare.]

440
00:30:54,960 --> 00:30:56,240
That wasn't...

441
00:30:57,510 --> 00:30:58,830
Why am I here?

442
00:30:58,920 --> 00:31:00,150
Why are you here?

443
00:31:00,500 --> 00:31:01,820
I heard you calling me,

444
00:31:01,910 --> 00:31:03,060
so I came to you.

445
00:31:03,490 --> 00:31:05,210
I saw you were having a nightmare.

446
00:31:05,610 --> 00:31:07,370
So I pulled you out from the dream.

447
00:31:08,070 --> 00:31:09,080
I was dreaming?

448
00:31:11,720 --> 00:31:16,340
Fali said

449
00:31:16,470 --> 00:31:18,810
that he agreed to let me see Kakarayan.

450
00:31:18,890 --> 00:31:20,480
And I went

451
00:31:20,610 --> 00:31:22,020
to the place where the dead go.

452
00:31:22,150 --> 00:31:23,160
That was all a dream?

453
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:27,650
Fali took you to see Kakarayan?

454
00:31:28,490 --> 00:31:29,230
Yes.

455
00:31:30,030 --> 00:31:31,300
He told me

456
00:31:31,960 --> 00:31:34,210
that I'd be able to meet Kakarayan

457
00:31:34,780 --> 00:31:36,580
if I went through the door.

458
00:31:40,540 --> 00:31:41,380
Then what happened?

459
00:31:42,870 --> 00:31:45,340
When I was about to walk
through that door,

460
00:31:45,470 --> 00:31:47,850
you suddenly told me
not to go any further.

461
00:31:47,930 --> 00:31:49,560
Then I realized

462
00:31:50,440 --> 00:31:53,610
the door that was supposed
to lead to Kakarayan

463
00:31:53,700 --> 00:31:56,690
turned into the place
that you told me about.

464
00:31:57,260 --> 00:31:59,550
The place where the dead go.

465
00:32:01,350 --> 00:32:02,100
Wait.

466
00:32:02,540 --> 00:32:04,960
You said that I told you
not to go further?

467
00:32:06,540 --> 00:32:07,250
Yes.

468
00:32:07,910 --> 00:32:10,110
Didn't you tell me not to enter that door?

469
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:11,470
I didn't.

470
00:32:12,570 --> 00:32:15,610
I just went into your dream
and got you out.

471
00:32:19,740 --> 00:32:21,060
Then who was that person?

472
00:32:45,260 --> 00:32:46,760
[Don't go any further.]

473
00:32:50,010 --> 00:32:51,110
I already told you.

474
00:32:51,200 --> 00:32:52,130
If you still won't deal
with Hsieh Tien-ti,

475
00:32:52,210 --> 00:32:54,060
I'll do it for you.

476
00:33:15,490 --> 00:33:16,900
You're not 'Orad.

477
00:33:26,360 --> 00:33:27,550
Kakarayan.

478
00:33:36,650 --> 00:33:38,190
Lemed, the god of dream.

479
00:33:40,220 --> 00:33:42,150
When will you understand

480
00:33:42,900 --> 00:33:45,800
why I gave you this name
in the first place?

481
00:34:03,180 --> 00:34:04,060
What about you?

482
00:34:06,620 --> 00:34:08,110
Why did you leave me?

483
00:34:12,820 --> 00:34:14,620
Why did you leave me?

484
00:34:16,870 --> 00:34:18,760
Why did you leave me?

485
00:34:23,030 --> 00:34:25,090
You brought me into your dream,

486
00:34:25,929 --> 00:34:27,780
but you left me alone!

487
00:34:28,130 --> 00:34:28,699
I...

488
00:34:48,590 --> 00:34:50,440
Kakarayan!

489
00:35:01,750 --> 00:35:03,810
Kakarayan!

490
00:35:28,450 --> 00:35:31,220
[Fali took you to see Kakarayan?]

491
00:35:31,360 --> 00:35:32,100
Yes.

492
00:35:32,900 --> 00:35:34,220
He told me

493
00:35:34,790 --> 00:35:36,900
that I'd be able to meet Kakarayan

494
00:35:37,030 --> 00:35:38,660
if I went through the door.

495
00:36:00,220 --> 00:36:01,670
Don't believe Fali.

496
00:36:02,020 --> 00:36:03,650
Just like you never believed me.
